			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove pub use re-exports from module public interfaces\n\nRemove wildcard and specific public re-exports from ApplicationState internal modules and the Air module. These re-exports were providing convenience access to internal types but violated encapsulation principles:\n\n- Air: Remove re-exports of AirClient, AirMetrics, AirStatus, and related types\n- ExtensionScanner: Remove ScanAndPopulateExtensions re-export\n- PathResolution: Remove ResolveMementoStorageFilePath re-export\n- Persistence: Remove MementoLoader and MementoSaver re-exports\n- Recovery: Remove RecoverState re-export\n- Serialization: Remove URLSerializer and URLDeserializer re-exports\n\nTypes should now be accessed via their explicit module paths rather than through re-exported shortcuts. This improves code clarity, prevents implicit dependencies, and enforces proper module boundaries.",
			"SHA": "8f12359311b56898cb7ee85280a905527c751ea4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-18T13:02:37Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				725,
				1
			],
			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Mountain into Current",
			"SHA": "b727de321fbc4c1d200579e8afdde7df5c191e10"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-18T13:02:35Z",
			"File": [
				"⣿⠁⠀⠀⠀",
				725,
				159
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Standardize dev_log! macro formatting across codebase\n\nReformat all dev_log! macro invocations from single-line to multi-line format for improved readability. This affects ~150+ call sites across Air, ApplicationState, Binary, Environment, IPC, RPC, RunTime, Telemetry, and Vine modules.\n\nAdditional improvements:\n- Add .js.map 204 handling in vscode-file scheme handler (DevTools compatibility)\n- Improve extension scanner logging for first-run scenarios (non-existent directory is debug-level, not warn)\n- Add NLS placeholder resolution logging to extension scanner\n\nNo functional changes aside from the DevTools .js.map fix and improved logging levels for first-run extension directories.",
			"SHA": "f0449be512c142adb02fd0397b03a2f4c5f79623"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Auto",
			"Date": "2026-04-18T01:59:36Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				691,
				1
			],
			"Message": "",
			"SHA": "1882da9ccc9697b2cc7a81986cc7516c05f7174f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-17T23:07:55Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				718,
				8
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Fix vscode-file:// URI resolution for extension assets\n\nAdd handling for absolute OS paths in the vscode-file:// scheme handler.\nVS Code extensions generate URIs like `vscode-file://vscode-app/Volumes/.../seti.woff`\nafter `FileAccess.uriToBrowserUri` rewrites extension paths. Detect common\nmacOS/Linux absolute path roots (Volumes, Users, Library, etc.) and serve\nfiles directly from disk instead of trying to resolve against Sky/Target.\n\nAlso add NLS placeholder resolution to the extension scanner. VS Code extensions\nuse `%key%` placeholders in package.json referencing `package.nls.json` entries.\nWithout this, the Command Palette and menus displayed literal `%command.clone%`,\n`%displayName%` strings. The scanner now loads NLS bundles and recursively replaces\nplaceholders in all string fields before parsing as ExtensionDescriptionStateDTO.\n\nAdditional improvements:\n- Downgrade benign \"Resource not found\" 404s in FileSystem.ReadFile to info-level\n  (extensions probe for optional cache files on activate)\n- Remove unused empty_ticks counter in Cocoon health monitor\n- Fix remaining PascalCase module references (ReadOperations, Messaging)\n- Simplify user extension path to only `.land/extensions`\n\nThese fixes enable proper loading of extension-contributed icon themes,\ngrammars, and localization.",
			"SHA": "336b21a62b258af6641298869881ccc293cd610c"
		}
	],
